<title>LATVIA: VENTSPILS NAFTA JUNE RELOADINGS EDGE UP.</title>
<headline>VENTSPILS NAFTA JUNE RELOADINGS EDGE UP.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reloadings of crude and oil products at Ventspils Nafta oil terminal, the leading Baltic outlet of Russian crude, rose to 2.1 million tonnes in June from two million tonnes in May.</p>
<p>It reloaded 1.2 million tonnes of crude, unchanged for the last three months, and 845,000 tonnes of diesel, a rise of 161,000 tonnes from May, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Venstpils said that diesel reloadings were close to this year's high of one million tonnes in March.</p>
<p>The volume of diesel with 0.05 percent sulphur content has doubled to 115,300 toness in June against 60,200 tonnes on May.</p>
<p>Ventspils said it has reloaded 13.06 million tonnes of crude and products in the first six months, a rise of 81,000 tonnes from the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>The terminal saw throughput of 7.3 million tonnes of crude and 4.8 million tonnes of diesel in the first six months.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
